{"name":"Zhū Hóng Vermillion","hex":"#cb464a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vermillion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of vermilion."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of vermilion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vermillion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Yunqi Zhuhong","blocks":[{"text":"Yunqi Zhuhong, also widely known as Master Lianchi, was a Chinese Buddhist monk during the late Ming Dynasty. The name Yunqi derives from his monastic residence on Mount Yunqi (雲棲山) hence \"Zhuhong of Yunqi [Mountain]\", while Lianchi translates to \"lotus pond\". In Chinese Buddhism, Yunqi Zhuhong is best remembered as the Eighth Patriarch of the Pure Land tradition, and is known for his analysis of the Pure Land thought, and reconciling \"mind-only\" interpretations with more literal \"Western Pure Land\" interpretations. Along with his lay follower, Yuan Hongdao, Zhuhong wrote extensively on the Pure Land and defended its tradition against other Buddhist critics, while analyzing the Pure Land of Amitabha Buddha within the larger Buddhist context."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/YunqiZhuhong2.jpg/330px-YunqiZhuhong2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yunqi_Zhuhong"},{"title":"Vermilion","blocks":[{"text":"Vermilion is a color family and toxic pigment most often used between antiquity and the 19th century and made from the powdered mineral cinnabar. It is synonymous with red orange."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Lacquerware-roundbox-w-children.jpg/330px-Lacquerware-roundbox-w-children.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vermilion"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Guanyin_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Guanyin_-_panoramio.jpg